# CodeQL SAST suppression list, honored by the fail-closed gate in
# .github/workflows/build-and-scan.yml ("Enforce CodeQL high-severity gate").
#
# A suppression silences ONE CodeQL ruleId that would otherwise block the build
# (level == "error" OR rule security-severity >= 7.0). It is deliberately strict
# and mirrors the .trivyignore VEX policy: an entry is honored ONLY when it has
# BOTH a justification AND a future expiry. Expired, unjustified, or malformed
# entries are ignored, so the finding keeps gating (fail-safe by design).
#
# Format (one rule per line):
#   <ruleId>  <justification text...>  expires=YYYY-MM-DD
#
# Example:
#   js/incomplete-sanitization  False positive: input is validated upstream by zod schema  expires=2026-09-01
#
# Rules:
#   - <ruleId> is the CodeQL rule id from the SARIF (e.g. js/sql-injection).
#   - The justification is mandatory free text explaining WHY this is safe to
#     suppress (not_affected / false_positive / accepted-with-compensating-control).
#   - expires= is mandatory and MUST be a future date; review and renew or remove
#     before it lapses. Once expired, the rule blocks again automatically.
#   - Suppressions are visible in the job log as ::notice:: lines for auditability.

# No active suppressions. The current app scans clean under security-extended.
